# Line endings.
#
# Everything here runs on Linux — in a container, or on the staging host. A
# CRLF shell script fails as `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or
# directory`, and a CRLF env file is worse than that: it fails silently.
# generate-staging-secrets.sh matches `^JWT_SECRET=$` to fill a secret in, and
# against a CRLF line the content is `JWT_SECRET=\r`, which matches nothing.
# The secret is never substituted, every downstream presence check passes
# because `\r` is not empty, and the stack boots with one-byte keys.
#
# Developers work on Windows, so this cannot be left to core.autocrlf.

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
.env.*.example  text eol=lf

# The deploy tree is executed verbatim on the staging host; nothing in it may
# carry a carriage return.
deploy/**       text eol=lf
